ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{50(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402287} {:answer/id #uuid "c0f34d3a-cfa0-5e02-8320-e125baa30770" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{50(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402288} {:answer/id #uuid "4a7ac352-d46a-51ed-a992-d68e07a53b35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{250(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402289}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a7ac352-d46a-51ed-a992-d68e07a53b35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{250(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402289} :answer-field/id #uuid "c69873a9-e21f-55cc-ba65-c7ed6f009b57" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402285}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "de25ec60-135e-5b0f-93ec-2a89a92381de" :question/math-academy-id "q-343341" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the $10$-periodic extension of the function $F(x)=5x$ defined on $[-5,5).$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below, showing the derivation of a series converging to the $10$-periodic extension of \n\n$$\nG(x)=\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{2}={\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nfrom the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x).$The Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n5x∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{50(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }{{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is \n{{field-2}} \non $R,$ we may integrate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{2}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{field-3}}\\cdot {{field-4}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $F(x)$ is an odd function. So, the Fourier series of its $2L$-periodic extension has the form\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=5$ and we are already given the coefficients ${b}_{n}$ for $n\\ge 1.$ Thus, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{50(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5}).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the function $F$ is continuous on $(-5,5).$ \nTherefore, the $10$-periodic extension $f$ is $\\text{piecewise continuous}$ on $R,$ so we may integrate its Fourier series term-by-term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}5t\\,\\text{d}t & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{50(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi t}{5})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ {[\\frac{5}{2}{t}^{2}]}_{0}^{x} & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{50(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\cdot [-\\frac{5}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi t}{5})]_{0}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}{x}^{2} & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{250(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\cdot (1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5}))\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402290 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b3cb7656-1ce6-5b6a-9e88-5ba24a943c3f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Value of an Infinite Sum Using Fourier Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8731841-813d-5c15-9844-bc300aded01c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1)^{n+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402292} {:answer/id #uuid "7d76bc51-9148-5c68-8eea-0c61f6eca229" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402293} {:answer/id #uuid "4b83a754-c4bd-58d7-824f-3b576edd0dbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402294} {:answer/id #uuid "152ee5ab-ddc5-54e1-abb5-85e05ecbc24d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1)^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402295}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d76bc51-9148-5c68-8eea-0c61f6eca229" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402293} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc21dfac-bf45-5494-902e-e23a4ab50c43" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402291} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71c7a223-28dd-5b98-95b8-adb22dcd23f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402297} {:answer/id #uuid "6acee3a9-dc08-557c-942a-b0c19f30c1c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402298} {:answer/id #uuid "d530070d-72ef-5bc5-ad66-9f775c9da2c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402299} {:answer/id #uuid "d2c4db87-8656-51bc-8c6d-365da5edd0c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402300}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71c7a223-28dd-5b98-95b8-adb22dcd23f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402297} :answer-field/id #uuid "98447180-9883-5216-9b4d-2f8d5e46c29a" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402296} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "acb22964-9386-55f3-b4ba-97747bec61c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402302} {:answer/id #uuid "4ff2de29-17f1-5bf9-b1b1-74047f493c81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402303} {:answer/id #uuid "c2980206-7d39-5dc7-9dd7-4a889845d7cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402304}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2980206-7d39-5dc7-9dd7-4a889845d7cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402304} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ab80b53-c5e0-529a-8043-c52969416199" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402301} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35eec229-a765-5483-a12b-af96b02f02b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "continuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402306} {:answer/id #uuid "c73e9609-34d2-5881-aad7-336bd7907eab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "discontinuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402307}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35eec229-a765-5483-a12b-af96b02f02b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "continuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402306} :answer-field/id #uuid "2793680d-49bf-5c9e-8ee3-c5e0e9eb684c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402305}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e361d1a0-a782-5eed-a0dc-4cde0324cd70" :question/math-academy-id "q-343395" :question/problem "Consider the function $F(x)=|x|$ defined on $x\\in [-2,2).$ The Fourier series of the $4$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼1-{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{8}{{\\pi }^{2}(2n-1)^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{(2n-1)\\pi }{2}x).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.At $x=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{(2n-1)\\pi }{2}\\cdot 0)={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is \n{{field-2}}\nat $x=0,$ the corresponding Fourier series converges to \n\n$$\nf(0)={{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(2n-1)^{2}}={{field-4}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite our Fourier series as\n\n$$\nf(x)∼1-\\frac{8}{{\\pi }^{2}}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(2n-1)^{2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{(2n-1)\\pi }{2}x).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that at $x=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{(2n-1)\\pi }{2}\\cdot 0)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)=1.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is $\\text{continuous}$ at $x=0,$ the corresponding Fourier series converges to \n\n$$\nf(0)=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0) & =1-\\frac{8}{{\\pi }^{2}}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(2n-1)^{2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{(2n-1)\\pi }{2}\\cdot 0) \\\\ 0 & =1-\\frac{8}{{\\pi }^{2}}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(2n-1)^{2}}\\cdot 1 \\\\ -1 & =-\\frac{8}{{\\pi }^{2}}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(2n-1)^{2}} \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(2n-1)^{2}} & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402308 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b3cb7656-1ce6-5b6a-9e88-5ba24a943c3f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Value of an Infinite Sum Using Fourier Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f6f980b-262a-50f0-ae3d-21301e83956a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1)^{n+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402310} {:answer/id #uuid "c9091f78-a863-5b79-82af-d78f1b7a6e0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402311} {:answer/id #uuid "ff2405a2-3755-5df5-98e5-3e6b5d35f747" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402312} {:answer/id #uuid "81d46c72-93bb-5c34-b05d-8f8e24f569a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1)^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402313}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81d46c72-93bb-5c34-b05d-8f8e24f569a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1)^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402313} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea007838-d48e-5282-9c26-7807b59be905" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402309} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bc209ef-e0e4-5126-a4d3-28477eac6672" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402315} {:answer/id #uuid "e1a6dfee-6b51-51e4-878f-80f01834b392" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.